{"name":"Frog Prince","hex":"#bbd75a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"frog","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of a class of small tailless amphibians of the order Anura that typically hop.","A member of this class that is not a toad."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt or trap frogs.","To use a pronged plater to transfer (cells) to another plate."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/frog"},{"term":"prince","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A (male) ruler, a sovereign; a king, monarch. .mw-parser-output .defdate{font-size:smaller}","A female monarch."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To behave or act like a prince.","To transform (someone) into a prince."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/prince"}],"entries":[{"title":"The Frog Prince","blocks":[{"text":"\"The Frog Prince; or, Iron Henry\" is a German fairy tale collected by the Brothers Grimm and published in 1812 in Grimms' Fairy Tales. Traditionally, it is the first story in their folktale collection. The tale is classified as Aarne-Thompson type 440."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/5/53/GmimmTheFrogPrince.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Frog_Prince","wikidata":"Q11850"},{"title":"Frog","blocks":[{"text":"A frog is any member of a diverse and largely semiaquatic group of short-bodied, tailless amphibian vertebrates composing the order Anura. Frog species with rough skin texture due to wart-like parotoid glands tend to be called toads, but the distinction between frogs and toads is informal and purely cosmetic, and does not reflect taxonomy or evolutionary history."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/Red-eyed_Leaf_Frog_%2849661076226%29.jpg/330px-Red-eyed_Leaf_Frog_%2849661076226%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frog","wikidata":"Q53636"},{"title":"Prince","blocks":[{"text":"A prince is a male ruler or a male member of a monarch's or former monarch's family. Prince is also a title of nobility, often hereditary, in some European states. The female equivalent is a princess. The English word derives, via the French word prince, from the Latin noun prīnceps, from primus (first) and caput (head), meaning \"the first, foremost, the chief, most distinguished, noble ruler, prince\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Prince_William_attends_Holocaust_Memorial_Day_%2854290704867%29%28cropped_3%29.jpg/330px-Prince_William_attends_Holocaust_Memorial_Day_%2854290704867%29%28cropped_3%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prince","wikidata":"Q2747456"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/The_Frog_Prince_-_Anne_Anderson.jpg/500px-The_Frog_Prince_-_Anne_Anderson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3e/The_Frog_Prince_-_Anne_Anderson.jpg/500px-The_Frog_Prince_-_Anne_Anderson.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Frog Prince by Anne Anderson","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AThe_Frog_Prince_-_Anne_Anderson.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/The_Princess_Meets_The_Frog_By_The_Fountain_-_Illustration_For_The_Frog_Prince_by_Walter_Crane_-_Walter_Crane_-_ABDAG003354.jpg/120px-The_Princess_Meets_The_Frog_By_The_Fountain_-_Illustration_For_The_Frog_Prince_by_Walter_Crane_-_Walter_Crane_-_ABDAG003354.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1e/The_Princess_Meets_The_Frog_By_The_Fountain_-_Illustration_For_The_Frog_Prince_by_Walter_Crane_-_Walter_Crane